ta-label pi-secondary-font\">Written by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"illustration\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Illustrated by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"colors\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Colors by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Miquel_Muerto\" title=\"Miquel Muerto\">Miquel Muerto</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"letters\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Lettered by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/AndWorld_Design\" title=\"AndWorld Design\">AndWorld Design</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"release_date\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Release date</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">March 18, 2020</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<table class=\"pi-horizontal-group\">\n\t<caption class=\"pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-secondary-background pi-item-spacing\">Chronology</caption>\n\t\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\">← Previous</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\">Next →</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t\n\t<tbody>\n\t<tr>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_5\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 5\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #5</a></td>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_7\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 7\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #7</a></td>\n\t\n\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #6</b> is a horror comic from <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a> that was published on March 18, 2020 by <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>. It is the sixth issue in the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">Something Is Killing the Children</a></i> comic series, the first issue of the five-part <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_House_of_Slaughter_(comic_arc)\" title=\"The House of Slaughter (comic arc)\">The House of Slaughter</a></i> arc, and the sixth issue of the fifteen-part <i>Archer's Peak</i> saga.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</span></h2>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica</a> may have slayed the beast terrorizing Archer's Peak, but the town is far from safe. As <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> recuperates from the horrible events of the last issue, Tommy also struggles to find his place in the new status quo of his life.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></p></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Plot\">Plot</span></h2>\n<p>The issue begins with <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> having a nightmare, remembering his last sleepover with his friends. He, <a href=\"/wiki/Karl\" title=\"Karl\">Karl</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Noah\" title=\"Noah\">Noah</a> and <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tyler (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVHlsZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Tyler</span> leave the house in order to find the monster James described. Noah sees the monster first, just as James trips and stumbles down the hill. He hears his friends scream.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> watches over a sleeping James in the hospital, as <a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a> approaches her. She says that it's up to James to report who shot him, and that she doesn't plan on telling him anything. When Tommy protests, Erica breaks his arm, and promises him that he does not want to know anything more than he's already seen. She then tells him to go out of state for a while, and he realizes that this isn't over.\n</p><p>At the den, <a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Joe Cavanaugh\">Joe</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Tim Cavanaugh\">Tim Cavanaugh</a> look over the pile of body parts. While Joe assures him that they won't get any media attention, Tim tells him that they won't be able to fit all of the bodies in the morgue, and that they're commandeering the school gymnasium. <a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer Richards</a> arrives unexpectedly and asks Joe what's going on. Joe tells him he doesn't know, and asks where <a href=\"/wiki/Bian\" title=\"Bian\">Bian</a> is. Richards realized someone has \"gotten to\" Joe, convincing him to keep quiet and not ask questions. \n</p><p>Erica approaches Bian at the police station, being watched over by a secretary named <a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a>; Bian invites her to draw with her. She tells Bian that something bad lives inside of <a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a>, and then looks at Bian's drawing of the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">monster's babies</span>. Bian tells her that the babies would eat the dead kids, while the mother would eat the live ones. Erica asks how many babies there were, and Bian says there were five. She says she is worried about the bodies being removed from the cave, as it means the babies wouldn't be able to eat; she then shows Erica a drawing of her killing the mother. Bian then looks at Erica's drawing of her house, and says that it looks scary.\n</p><p>At the House of Slaughter, <a href=\"/wiki/Cecilia_Slaughter\" title=\"Cecilia Slaughter\">Cecilia Slaughter</a> tells <a href=\"/wiki/Aaron_Slaughter\" title=\"Aaron Slaughter\">Aaron</a> that <a href=\"/wiki/The_Old_Dragon\" title=\"The Old Dragon\">The Old Dragon</a> has ordered him to go to Archer's Peak to deal with Erica's mess. Aaron argues that this isn't his fault, as Erica has never followed orders well. Cecilia tells him that the Dragon expects the two of them to both be grown-up now. She orders Aaron to relieve Erica of her duty, and finish the job himself. He says that she won't return, and Cecilia tells him that any further breaking of protocol will be his fault. She then tells him to kill Tommy Mahoney, as the House of Slaughter will not take in another stray like Erica.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Characters\">Characters</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Order_of_St._George\"><a href=\"/wiki/Order_of_St._George\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Order of St. George\">Order of St. George</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Aaron_Slaughter\" title=\"Aaron Slaughter\">Aaron Slaughter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Cecilia_Slaughter\" title=\"Cecilia Slaughter\">Cecilia Slaughter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Archer.27s_Peak\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Archer's_Peak\"><a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Joe Cavanaugh\">Sheriff Joe Cavanaugh</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Tim Cavanaugh\">Tim Cavanaugh</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Karl\" title=\"Karl\">Karl</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tyler_Monitz\" title=\"Tyler Monitz\">Tyler Monitz</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Noah\" title=\"Noah\">Noah</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer John Richards</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Monsters\">Monsters</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratypes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Oscuratypes\">Oscuratypes</a>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype children</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype mother (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfbW90aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype mother</span> †</li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>Despite being named as \"John\" in a previous issue, Officer Richards is referred to as \"Tom\" in this issue. This is what he is referred to for the rest of the series.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comic_guide\">Comic guide</span></h2>\n<table class=\"navbar mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"Expand\" data-collapsetext=\"Collapse\" width=\"100%\" style=\"border: 1px solid #8c8c8c; background:transparent; border-radius:4px; text-align:center;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"background: var(--theme-sticky-nav-background-color); border-radius:4px;\" align=\"left\"><div style=\"height:3px; margin:0px 0px 0px 3px\"><div style=\"font-size:8pt\"><a href=\"/wiki/Template:Comic_(SIKTC)\" title=\"Template:Comic (SIKTC)\">v</a> • <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://something-is-killing-the-children.fandom.com/wiki/Template_talk:Comic_(SIKTC)\">d</a> • <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://something-is-killing-the-children.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Comic_(SIKTC)?veaction=editsource\">e</a></div></div> <center><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_comics\" title=\"Category:Something Is Killing the Children comics\"><font color=\"#E7F0DF\">Comic guide</font></a></center>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"background: var(--theme-sticky-nav-background-color); border-radius:4px;\"><font color=\"#E7F0DF\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Angel_of_Archer%27s_Peak_(comic_arc)\" title=\"The Angel of Archer&#39;s Peak (comic arc)\">Volume 1: <i>The Angel of Archer's Peak</i></a></font>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_1\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 1\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #1</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_2\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 2\">#2</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_3\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 3\">#3</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_4\" title=\"Something Is Killing the